For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since they are code

For applications, you'll usually want to keep them. See: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/master/Python.gitignore

.python-version

pipenv

According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to checkin Pipfile.lock into version control.

However, in some cases federated projects might be better off not including it.

Pipfile.lock

Poetry

Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to checkin poetry.lock into version control.

This is a personal preference depending on whether you want to track dependencies.

poetry.lock

pdm

Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to checkin pdm.lock into version control.

